new specs and real Chrome/Edge, fixtures lack the users and states the ACs need, and server logs are not test-readable.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:82:Reasoning: Review r1 #12: closing the shared socket cannot 
prove independent stream failures; the banner, polling, and typing ACs need a proven per-topic fault method.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:109:Reasoning: Review r1 #3, #14: fenced recovery is a separate 
failure surface from durable enqueue, and AC-040 needs it.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:190:Reasoning: The user-facing mention flow on top of T4, for both 
queued text and unqueued attachment/voice sends.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:191:Task: Typing "@" opens an accessible combobox/listbox of the 
conversation's current members (T4 roster) except the user, filtered while typing, operable by arrows/Enter/Tab/Esc 
and mouse; choosing inserts a highlighted mention whose user ID travels with the send — in the outbox item for text 
and in the create request for attachment/voice messages (including their Phase 4 retry); unselected "@name" text is 
plain; mentions render distinctly for everyone and the mentioned viewer sees the whole message highlighted with a 
non-color cue; a stale poll never drops a mention delivered by Realtime.
