(delayed `check_rate_limit('message:create',1,5)` returned true); the in-transaction response test failed on r1 
(stored message left behind after a 500).
102:- Performer (final): budgets 15/15; budgets+fencing+idempotency+attachments 60/60; `npm run test:messaging:db` 
87/88 (known message-readers Realtime flake; rerun of that file 4/4) then 88/88; `npm run test:messaging:local:e2e` 
51/51 (98 creates, no 429); type-check clean; eslint 0 problems in changed lines. Header rollback executed for real 
for r0, r1 and r2 locally (restored the T2 state and the verbatim limiter body), then reapplied.
103:- Supabase/RLS review gate (supabase-rls-reviewer, three passes) → no blocker/major. r0: header statement-timeout 
claim corrected (lock timeout/deadlock → 429; statement_timeout → 500 with nothing stored); counter-row serialization 
accepted (last lock taken). r1: unkeyed readback 500 risk (→ fixed in r2); legacy 500 when a reply target is deleted 
mid-request rejected (unchanged legacy status, nothing stored or charged); rollback INSERT grant verified faithful to 
the pre-T3 catalog. r2: malformed-row fallback read added (note 1); INSERT_QUOTA_INVALID documented (note 2); a Phase 
5 insertion waiting on the per-user lock while holding row locks accepted (latency only, bounded by budgets).
104:- Adversarial review r1 (reviews/sol-review-t3-r1.md; gpt-6.1-sol, max) → revision required. High 1 direct unkeyed 
inserts bypass budgets → fixed (policy dropped, INSERT revoked). Medium 2 minute rollover reopens an exhausted quota → 
fixed (quota helper: per-user lock, clock window after the lock). Medium 3 failed unkeyed inserts charged → fixed 
(unkeyed via the transactional function). Medium 4 broad 42501 → 403 → fixed (exact marker). Low 5 rollback order 
outage → fixed (app first, then SQL).
105:- Adversarial review r2 (reviews/sol-review-t3-r2.md; gpt-6.1-sol, max) → revision required. Medium 1 Phase 4 
check_rate_limit charges outside the serialization → fixed (delegation + mixed-writer regression + verbatim rollback). 
Medium 2 unkeyed post-commit readback → duplicate-producing 500 → fixed (row returned from the transaction). Low 3 
rollover test lock detection could pick an unrelated backend → fixed (`waitForBlockedBy(holderPid, waiterPid)` with 
pg_blocking_pids).
109:- [verified] public.messages has no client INSERT path; every message write goes through service-role routes and 
`create_message_attempt` → affects T4 (mentions must be written inside that function's transaction), T8+.
110:- [verified] `create_message_attempt` returns the created row as `message` when created → affects T4, T7 (mapper 
reuse).
