> spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:9:## Standing rules for every task
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:10:
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:11:- **Migration rule (BR-014, AC-034):** during the phase a 
migration is done when it is written, applied to the LOCAL database, its tests pass, and its rollback SQL is recorded 
in the migration header and TRACK. Each one gets a row in 
`spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/MIGRATIONS-PENDENTES.md`. Nothing is applied online before T23.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:12:- **Old-build compatibility at introduction (§10):** every 
task that changes a DB contract or a route proves, with integration tests against the migrated local DB, that the 
hosted pre-Phase-4 client contract (unkeyed creates) and the Phase 4 client contract (keyed text/attachment/voice 
creates and their replays, without the new fields) keep working; T21 repeats this as a combined smoke with the real 
old builds.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:13:- **Online application method (T23 only):** the Phase 4 
method (Phase 4 TRACK T2/T25): re-check `npx supabase migration list --linked` and the target catalog immediately 
before; apply only each reviewed file's SQL transactionally and record only its version; read back by statement hash 
plus catalog objects; smoke-check. Never `supabase db push`, `migration up --linked`, or broad `migration repair`.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:14:- **Supabase/RLS review gate (AC-035):** every migration, 
RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API route change passes the `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit (users.id vs 
supabase_uid, server client + `auth.getUser()`, service role never replacing membership checks) before the task is 
done.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:15:- **Adversarial review gate (AGENTS.md):** each task's diff 
gets the cross-model adversarial review (direct Codex CLI, `gpt-6.1-sol`, effort `max`, read-only, per 
`delegation-anthropic.md`) before it is recorded done; findings fixed or rejected with reasons in TRACK. The whole 
work-item diff gets the same review in T22.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:16:- **Test policy (BR-015, AC-036):** integration tests against 
local Supabase/Realtime/real routes and Playwright E2E only. T1–T6 run their regression E2E through the existing local 
runner (`npm run test:messaging:local:e2e`); from T24 on, every E2E gate runs through the T24 runner (local Supabase; 
real Chrome and Edge projects); no unit tests; a touched unit test is replaced and deleted, recorded in TRACK. A new 
E2E spec counts only after 3 consecutive passing runs in Chrome and in Edge with zero retries, zero flaky, and no 
skipped critical test. Network shaping only (SPEC §15); no mocked Supabase, repositories, or code under test.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:17:- **Regression (FR-032, AC-033):** every task that changes 
server or drawer behavior ends with the messaging DB integration suite and the messaging regression E2E suite passing 
locally, plus type-check and lint.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:18:- **Presence touch points:** any change near sign-out or 
Realtime lifecycle follows the `presence-safety` skill; the Presence logout sequence is unchanged.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:19:- **Planning decisions under D4 (owner-adjustable):** budget 
infrastructure fails closed — if a create, fence, or metrics budget cannot be checked, the request is refused as a 
transient 429 (the outbox retries it) instead of being allowed; Phase 4 keyed requests that carry no attempt 
generation keep the Phase 4 keyed contract (create, replay 200, 409) and take part in the same commit-time exclusion 
as fencing: such a request commits only if no fence state exists for its key at commit time, where fence state is 
created only by a fence call or a generation-carrying request (a generation-less create creates none, so Phase 4 
retries are unaffected); a generation-less request that loses to a fence stores nothing and is rejected as stale. 
Per-stream Realtime faults in E2E may inject Phoenix channel frames (`phx_error`, `phx_close`) or withhold a single 
topic's replies on the real socket; this counts as network shaping of a single stream (SPEC §15) — the real transport, 
joins, and application callbacks stay in place and no application health is set directly; a real server mechanism is 
preferred where one exists.
> spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:36:## T4 — Server-validated atomic mentions and current-member 
roster
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:37:Reasoning: Mentions are a data contract consumed by composer 
and notifications on both create paths; the autocomplete needs a current roster no existing read provides.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:38:Task: A mention store holds application user IDs mentioned by 
a message, written in the same transaction as the first creation on both the text path and the attachment/voice path 
(since T3 every message insert — keyed, unkeyed, Phase 4 wrapper — runs inside `create_message_attempt`, and clients 
have no INSERT on public.messages), only for conversation members at that time other than the sender; requested 
mention IDs are part of the stored original composition (changed mentions on replay → 409; unchanged replay after a 
recipient left returns the stored message); only members can read mention records; no client can write them; messages 
fetched by members carry their mention IDs. An authorized read returns a conversation's current members (from 
`conversation_members`, so removed members are excluded) to members only.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:39:Done when: The AC-024 server clauses, the AC-046 replay 
clause, and the roster contract hold on the local database for both create paths.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:40:Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests: non-member and 
self IDs store nothing; changed-mention replay 409 with no change; forced mention-storage failure stores neither 
message, attachment links, nor mentions (text and attachment paths); anon/non-member read denied; direct client writes 
denied; unchanged replay after removal returns stored message; roster excludes a removed member and is denied to 
non-members; Phase 4/legacy compatibility passes; RLS review gate recorded.
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:41:Covers: FR-023, FR-024, BR-010, AC-024, AC-046, AC-035
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:42:Root: T4
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:43:Depends on: T2
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:44:
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:45:## T28 — Membership integrity: memberships only through 
authorized server paths
  spec-interview\phase-5-messaging-resilience\PLAN.md:46:Reasoning: Every members-only guarantee of this phase (typing 
topic, mentions, roster, read state, messages, attachments, receipts) trusts `conversation_members`; owner decision D9 
puts the self-enrolment gap in scope (PLAN review r4 #1–#3 widened it to every client-reachable and server-side path 
that creates or restores a membership).
